---
import './operations.css';
---
<figure class="ops-figure" data-ops-failover>
 <figcaption><span>Figure 3</span> The endpoint returns; the old price returns too</figcaption>
 <div class="ops-scene">
  <div class="copies" data-live>
   <div data-node="source"><b>Authoritative source</b><span class="card" data-card="source">P7 · GBP 20.00</span><small data-revision="source">Revision 1</small></div>
   <div data-node="primary"><b>Redis primary</b><span class="card" data-card="primary">P7 · GBP 20.00</span><small data-revision="primary">Revision 1</small></div>
   <div data-node="replica"><b data-role>Redis replica</b><span class="card" data-card="replica">P7 · GBP 20.00</span><small>Revision 1 · not expired</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="replication" data-live><span data-link>Primary → replica: asynchronous copies</span><b data-delete>Deletion not sent yet</b></div>
  <div class="reader" data-live><b>App A</b><span data-answer>No read in progress</span></div>
  <p class="ops-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Both cache copies hold the original card.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="ops-controls"><div class="ops-buttons"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span></div><div class="ops-hold" data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <p class="ops-caption">One possible order under asynchronous replication, drawn from Redis’s documented behaviour; no failover was executed for this figure. The elapsed time stays within the entry’s expiry. P7 abbreviates the north shop’s en-GB, GBP product-card key.</p>
 <details><summary>Failover as text</summary><ol><li>Source, primary and replica hold revision 1.</li><li>The source commits revision 2 at GBP 22.00.</li><li>The primary acknowledges deleting the cached card. The replica has not applied the deletion.</li><li>The primary fails. The replica becomes primary and App A reconnects.</li><li>A lookup finds revision 1. A reader requiring revision 2 rejects it and uses the bounded source path.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-ops-failover]').forEach(root=>{
 const set=(selector:string,value:string)=>root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent=value;
 const primary=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-node="primary"]')!;
 const card=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-card="replica"]')!;
 let previous=-1;let animation:Animation|undefined;
 const explanations=[
 'The source and both cache copies agree on revision 1. Replication has caught up at this starting point.',
 'The source commits GBP 22.00 at revision 2. Neither cached copy has changed yet.',
 'The primary applies DEL and replies successfully. Its replica has not received the deletion. The two cached states now differ.',
 'The primary fails before the deletion reaches the replica. After promotion and client reconnection, the new endpoint still holds revision 1.',
 'App A reads GBP 20.00 from the new primary. For a read requiring revision 2 or newer, this is an unusable hit. The source path still needs admission and remaining time.'
 ];
 const draw=(step:number)=>{
  set('[data-card="source"]',step?'P7 · GBP 22.00':'P7 · GBP 20.00');set('[data-revision="source"]',step?'Revision 2':'Revision 1');
  set('[data-card="primary"]',step>=3?'Unavailable':step>=2?'No entry':'P7 · GBP 20.00');set('[data-revision="primary"]',step>=3?'Connection lost':step>=2?'DEL acknowledged':'Revision 1');
  set('[data-role]',step>=3?'Promoted primary':'Redis replica');primary.classList.toggle('failed',step>=3);
  set('[data-link]',step>=3?'Old primary → replica: link lost':'Primary → replica: asynchronous copies');
  set('[data-delete]',step>=2?'DEL did not reach this copy':'Deletion not sent yet');
  set('[data-answer]',step===4?'GET finds revision 1 → reject for a revision 2 read':step===3?'Reconnect to the promoted primary':'No read in progress');
  root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=explanations[step];
  if(previous!==step){animation?.cancel();if(step===4&&!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches){const destination=root.querySelector('.reader')!.getBoundingClientRect(),from=card.getBoundingClientRect();animation=card.animate([{transform:'translateY(0)'},{transform:`translateY(${destination.top-from.bottom-8}px)`,offset:.6},{transform:'translateY(0)'}],{duration:1100,easing:'ease-in-out'});}previous=step;}
 };
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw});
});
</script>
<style>
.copies{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem}.copies>div{padding:.7rem .45rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface);text-align:center}.copies b,.copies small{display:block}.copies b{min-height:2.7rem;font-size:.82rem}.card{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border:2px solid var(--teal);border-radius:4px;min-height:56px;margin:.5rem 0;background:var(--color-surface);font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);position:relative;z-index:2}.failed{border-style:dashed!important}.failed .card{border-style:dashed;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.replication{padding:1rem .4rem;text-align:center}.replication span,.replication b{display:block}.replication b{font-weight:500;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.reader{border:2px solid var(--teal);padding:.7rem;background:var(--color-surface);display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:center}.reader b{white-space:nowrap}.reader span{font-size:.85rem}@media(max-width:500px){.copies{gap:.3rem}.copies>div{padding:.5rem .2rem}.copies b{font-size:.76rem}.card{font-size:.76rem}.reader{align-items:flex-start}}
</style>
